# Append-only log files: two branches each appending new lines should merge as the
# union of both sides' lines, never as a text conflict. Safe here specifically because
# every consumer (tools/agent-monitoring/{generate_retro,query,validate}.py, and the
# agent-ops-dashboard ingest design) reads these by explicit ts/seq/run_id fields, never
# by physical line position — see conversation 2026-07-16 for the verification.
#
# CAVEAT (TCK-20260906-WORKING-LOG-MERGE-UNION-DUPLICATION-GAP): merge=union only
# engages when git's own merge machinery actually runs (`git merge`, `git rebase`,
# `git cherry-pick -m`, GitHub's "Create a merge commit" option) — it does NOT protect
# against a GitHub squash-merge, which this repo's PRs use almost exclusively (5/5 of
# the last 5 merged PRs sampled were squash-merged; a squash-merge has exactly one
# parent and applies a plain diff, invoking no merge driver at all). This gap already
# produced one confirmed ~1586-row whole-block duplication in tickets/working_log.csv
# (see investigation.md for that ticket). The actual squash-merge-safe protection is
# tests/integrity/test_no_duplicate_content_blocks.py, which detects (not prevents)
# any new duplicate content block landing via this path.
agent-monitoring/data/*/*.jsonl merge=union
tickets/working_log.csv merge=union

# docs/REGISTRY.yaml is deliberately NOT listed here: it's a full-file rewrite on every
# Finalize (not an append), so union-merging two independent regenerations could produce
# invalid YAML. Resolve conflicts there by taking either side and rerunning
# `make docs-registry`, not by hand-merging the diff.
